-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Smash TV
  Publisher   Ocean, 1991
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Smash TV (1991)(Ocean)(128K).z80
  MD5         78a6c5b03168844bbe0cca20770e5891

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz; works on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11).
              1.2: the game now holds the original's pace; 1.1 ran about 7%
              slower everywhere.

  Note        Known issues: pace against the original in JNext, 4 runs of 600
              updates with the same input and game state equal at every
              update: overall -0.30 to -0.27%, quiet scenes -0.34 to -0.23%,
              busy scenes -0.26 to -0.19%, stretches of 20 updates -1.0 to
              +0.6% (1.1: overall +7.1 to +7.8%, slowest stretch +9.4%). These
              runs are arena 1 only, by script; later arenas and the bosses
              are not measured. One recorded play path runs Next ROM routines
              that differ from the 48K ROM's, and the game reads a few ROM
              bytes as data (found by replay; JNext reached play; effect on
              play not established). Missing: no Enhanced colour set; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

